# LUCOST AI real worker (not yet able to make AI video)

This is the real worker's structure: it reads the job, splits nothing itself (the app splits the script),
builds each spoken line with the voice and face models, joins the lines, uploads the part to R2, and returns video_url.

## Status
- **Voice, face, and lip-sync models: not chosen.** Each stage raises ModelNotConfigured, so a job returns
  a clear error instead of a fake video. Nothing is faked.
- **Licences:** a model is only plugged in after its licence allows commercial use. Check each one first.

## Plugging in a model (after the licence check)
1. Set VOICE_MODEL, FACE_MODEL, LIPSYNC_MODEL in RunPod's environment variables.
2. Implement that model's call in models.py (synthesize_speech / animate_face).
3. Test one 30-second scene and measure GPU time, then update config.py.

## Deploy
Same as the test worker: its own repository, with Dockerfile, handler.py, models.py, requirements.txt.
Set R2_ACCOUNT_ID, R2_ACCESS_KEY, R2_SECRET_KEY, R2_BUCKET, R2_PUBLIC_URL in RunPod.
